*HEADING
Project 05 V6b: linear buckling of the restrained plate, preload = mechanical equivalent of a 1 K uniform temperature rise (prescribed mean edge displacement)
** SI units (m, kg, s, N, Pa); no temperature loading anywhere in this deck
*INCLUDE, INPUT=../../mesh/v_n40_z2.inp
*INCLUDE, INPUT=../../mesh/v_n40_z2_framepre.inp
*NSET, NSET=FRAME_ALL
FRAME_X0, FRAME_X1, FRAME_Y0, FRAME_Y1
*MATERIAL, NAME=TI64
*ELASTIC
113.8E9, 0.33
*SOLID SECTION, ELSET=PANEL, MATERIAL=TI64
** out-of-plane support on the four mid-thickness edge lines; in-plane restraint from the equations
*BOUNDARY
FRAME_ALL, 3, 3
** step 1: preload (prescribed mean edge displacement = free thermal expansion for 1 K, linear static)
*STEP
*STATIC
1., 1., 1.E-5, 1.
*INCLUDE, INPUT=../../mesh/v_n40_z2_framepre_bc.inp
*EL PRINT, ELSET=PANEL
S
*NODE PRINT, NSET=FACE_X0, TOTALS=ONLY
RF
*NODE PRINT, NSET=FACE_Y0, TOTALS=ONLY
RF
*END STEP
** step 2: buckling factors = multiples of the preload (= critical temperature rise in K)
*STEP
*BUCKLE
6
*NODE PRINT, NSET=TOP
U
*END STEP
